      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Top-Hat-Rogers-Astaire.jpg",
      "heading": "A dance that never stops — stopped",
      "body": [
        {
          "kicker": "Describe",
          "text": "Look at the bodies, the gown, the light and the crop. Follow the line of the dress: where does it go, and where does it stop?"
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Production",
          "text": "This is a studio publicity photograph from 1935, not a frame of the film. Who posed it, and for whom?"
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Critical",
          "text": "She leans back and he holds her. What does the photograph freeze that the dance itself would never stop on?"
        }
      ],
      "image_brief": "Ginger Rogers and Fred Astaire in a Top Hat publicity still: the feathered sleeve spreads like a fan.",
      "notes": "- Model the first block aloud; pairs do the rest."
    },
