      "heading": "1 · The cloth arrives after the body",
      "sentence": "When a dancer moves, the fabric follows a moment later — and as we watch, we feel that movement in our own body.",
      "prompt": "Very little film of Isadora Duncan dancing is known: her dance reaches us mostly through photographs.",
      "image_brief": "Arnold Genthe's photograph of Isadora Duncan in a loose tunic, one arm raised.",
      "notes": "- Play the Muybridge loop in the lesson: the hem lands after the step.",
      "quote": "we map these postures and gestures onto our own body, feeling them in our own skin and bones",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Shinkle 2008, 222)",
