      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Museo del Traje - MT111885 - Vestido Delphos.jpg",
      "heading": "2 · Two artists borrow ancient Greece",
      "sentence": "Isadora Duncan danced in loose “Greek” tunics, and the designer Mariano Fortuny, born in Granada, pleated silk into a column he called Delphos.",
      "prompt": "This Delphos gown is in the Museo del Traje in Madrid. Whose “classical” body becomes the ideal — and who is left out?",
      "image_brief": "Fortuny's black Delphos gown, Museo del Traje, Madrid: pleats that open only when a body moves.",
      "notes": "- Drape: the garment follows and lengthens the gesture.\n- A revival is not the ancient practice itself."
    },
